# {{ appTitle }}

App key: `{{ appKey }}`. Composer package: `{{ packageComposerName }}`.
PHP namespace: `{{ packageNamespace }}`; PSR-4 source: `src/`.

Read AGENTS.md and the design records in docs/. Install the public dependencies
with Composer and npm in this App directory. The platform operator provides
the Nexia Sandbox; this repository contains no Core installation.

## Connect and run

This App belongs in an immediate child folder of a Nexia project. From the parent
project folder, run `nexia connect <project-id>` and approve in the browser. From
this App, install dependencies and create your first resource:

```sh
composer install --no-scripts
npm install
nexia make resource Note --label-ko '메모'
nexia dev
```

`dev` watches the entire project even from an App subdirectory. Use `--app` to
select one App. It registers identities, prepares the personal sandbox, syncs
source and watches React builds. All Apps share one port. `nexia login` renews
project authentication without changing bindings. Missing creation settings are
prompted; options skip matching questions. `--no-interactive --yes` is available
for explicit automation, not for bypassing platform approval.

Open the printed workspace URL. Grant the App's test read/create/update
permissions in Developers, save a record and reopen it to verify persistence.
Registration grants no business access. `nexia make page ExamplePage` adds a page
without creating a model or migration; implement its business query.

## Docker tools

The generated Dockerfile and Compose service retain the App tooling environment.
Set NEXIA_UID/NEXIA_GID on macOS/Linux to your user/group IDs when needed.

```sh
docker compose build dev
docker compose run --rm --service-ports --entrypoint sh dev
```

Inside the container, install App dependencies and use `nexia login <project-id>`.
Open the printed URL manually. A registered standalone App can run
`nexia dev --container`. For a new App, register through project `dev` first or
mount/connect the complete project with its Apps. An unregistered App-only mount
is not a project workspace. Credentials remain private in the container volume;
do not copy them from the host or remove the volume to restart development.
An operator-supplied alternate origin can be selected using NEXIA_ENDPOINT before
login/connection; an existing project keeps its bound origin.

## Checks

```sh
nexia check
composer install --no-scripts
composer test
```

`nexia check` parses source without running App code. The generated resource
test checks its authorization declaration; add App-owned behavior tests for
real data and permissions. Composer tests execute your App test code. Do not
point local tests at a tenant database. Core's test classes are not dependencies.
Frontend tests use `npm test` after installing dependencies; add actual test
files before using that result as evidence.

`nexia dev` builds and watches the App's React entry in `dist/frontend/`, including
lazy surface chunks and a Vite manifest. SDK/React peers remain external for the
Nexia host; this output is not a standalone HTML preview. The build does not load
`.env` files or copy `public/`. Import browser assets explicitly from frontend
source. Never import secrets or PHP files. Building executes your Vite config
and dependencies; it is separate from the non-executing `nexia check` check.

With Docker, install in the same mounted App directory using
`docker compose run --rm --entrypoint npm dev install`. Keep the generated
package lock in your repository. Local builds require Node.js 22.12 or later and npm 11.6.2 (11.x).
Without changing your global npm installation, run
`npm exec --yes --package=npm@11.6.2 -- npm install` to create the lock.
The generated Docker image already includes this npm version.

Resource generation creates PHP/React application screens. The public CLI does
not expose force-overwrite or Filament generation options. Existing PHP devtools
capabilities remain available to their existing callers.

Before submission, commit/push source and a version tag with Git. Run
`nexia check`, `nexia submit --tag v1.0.0`, then `nexia submit status <id>`.
Repository connection is requested in Developers when needed. Submission is not
publication or installation. For App database work use `nexia db migrate`,
`nexia db seed`, and `nexia db status`; queued does not mean completed.
